{
  "schema_version": "argument_graph/0.1",
  "example_id": "persuade:45C70D14F6F3",
  "root": "u5",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "u1",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 95,
      "text": "The electoral college was a great attempt to give a reliable system of selecting the president,",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u2",
      "start": 96,
      "end": 164,
      "text": "but it just does not work the way our founding fathers wanted it to.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u3",
      "start": 165,
      "end": 237,
      "text": "Many people throughout the country have brought this up as a major issue",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u4",
      "start": 238,
      "end": 262,
      "text": "because they also agree.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u5",
      "start": 263,
      "end": 366,
      "text": "The other option that people would prefer to have would be selecting the president by the popular vote,",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u6",
      "start": 367,
      "end": 393,
      "text": "which is the smarter path.",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u7",
      "start": 394,
      "end": 425,
      "text": "This method is more democratic,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u8",
      "start": 426,
      "end": 482,
      "text": "it has a smaller chance of producing unreliable results,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u9",
      "start": 483,
      "end": 586,
      "text": "and it  encourages voters to still vote in states where there is already a predominant political party.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u10",
      "start": 588,
      "end": 628,
      "text": "The electoral college is not democratic.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u11",
      "start": 629,
      "end": 727,
      "text": "The method of selecting people for it is generally controlled by each candidate's political party,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u12",
      "start": 728,
      "end": 787,
      "text": "and their responsibilities vary based on the party's wants.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u13",
      "start": 788,
      "end": 890,
      "text": "The people who select the candidates for the electoral college are not part of the popular population;",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u14",
      "start": 891,
      "end": 926,
      "text": "they are part of a political party.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u15",
      "start": 927,
      "end": 974,
      "text": "Next, when people go to vote for the president,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u16",
      "start": 975,
      "end": 1013,
      "text": "they are not voting for the president,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u17",
      "start": 1014,
      "end": 1100,
      "text": "but actually voting for a slate of electors that in their turn vote for the president.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u18",
      "start": 1101,
      "end": 1181,
      "text": "And to take this to the next step, as shown in \"What Is the Electoral College?\",",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u19",
      "start": 1182,
      "end": 1290,
      "text": "\"Most states have a winner-takes-all system that awards all electors to the winning presidential candidate.\"",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u20",
      "start": 1291,
      "end": 1344,
      "text": "If voters vote for the candidate that ends up losing,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u21",
      "start": 1345,
      "end": 1395,
      "text": "poof, all their votes are given to the other team.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u22",
      "start": 1396,
      "end": 1436,
      "text": "To atleast make this a little more fair,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u23",
      "start": 1437,
      "end": 1473,
      "text": "instead of voting for the president,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "rejected",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u24",
      "start": 1474,
      "end": 1567,
      "text": "voters should cast votes for the electoral college members that are choosing their president.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u25",
      "start": 1568,
      "end": 1651,
      "text": "That way, you can at least do research on the people whom you are really voting for",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u26",
      "start": 1652,
      "end": 1688,
      "text": "and make the best decision possible.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u27",
      "start": 1690,
      "end": 1763,
      "text": "The popular vote is the most reliable way to get results from the people.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u28",
      "start": 1764,
      "end": 1857,
      "text": "It is the most raw, unbreakable way of selecting the highest political figure of the country.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u29",
      "start": 1858,
      "end": 1961,
      "text": "On the other hand, the electoral college's slight stretches have the possibility of unreliable results.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u30",
      "start": 1962,
      "end": 2081,
      "text": "In \"The Indefensible Electoral College: Why even the best-laid defenses of the system are wrong\", it becomes known that",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u31",
      "start": 2082,
      "end": 2164,
      "text": "\"...thanks to the quirks of the electoral college - [Al Gore] won the popular vote",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u32",
      "start": 2165,
      "end": 2190,
      "text": "but lost the presidency\".",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u33",
      "start": 2191,
      "end": 2214,
      "text": "It is still argued that",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u34",
      "start": 2215,
      "end": 2501,
      "text": "the electoral members chosen are extremely trustworthy :\"each party selects a state of electors trusted to vote for the party's nominee (and that trust is rarely betrayed)\" (from \"In defense of the Electoral College: Five reasons to keep our despised method of choosing the President\").",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u35",
      "start": 2502,
      "end": 2603,
      "text": "However, even in the continuation of the fragment above, even Richard A. Posner (,the author,) admits",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u36",
      "start": 2604,
      "end": 2711,
      "text": "\"[;however,] it is entirely possible that the winner of the electoral vote will not win the national vote.\"",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u37",
      "start": 2712,
      "end": 2791,
      "text": "The electoral college members are trusted to vote for whom they were voted for,",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u38",
      "start": 2792,
      "end": 2855,
      "text": "but their job is to be a highly knowledgeable political expert;",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u39",
      "start": 2856,
      "end": 2911,
      "text": "and if they see the other president as a better choice,",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u40",
      "start": 2912,
      "end": 2943,
      "text": "then it can become very unfair.",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u41",
      "start": 2945,
      "end": 3049,
      "text": "The electoral college discourages people to vote in countries where there is already a dominating party.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u42",
      "start": 3050,
      "end": 3198,
      "text": "For example, California is mostly a democratic country that usually casts a (highly populated) vote for the democratic party's electoral candidates.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u43",
      "start": 3199,
      "end": 3254,
      "text": "So why should republicans consider voting in this area?",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u44",
      "start": 3255,
      "end": 3324,
      "text": "The government has always tried to push out that \"every vote counts\",",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u45",
      "start": 3325,
      "end": 3353,
      "text": "but is this really the case?",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u46",
      "start": 3354,
      "end": 3517,
      "text": "Another good point of this is explained by Bradford Plumer again in \"The Indefensible Electoral College: Why even the best laid defenses of the system are wrong\" :",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u47",
      "start": 3518,
      "end": 3571,
      "text": "\"Because of the winner-take-all system in each state,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u48",
      "start": 3572,
      "end": 3651,
      "text": "candidates don't spend time in states they know they have no chance of winning,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u49",
      "start": 3652,
      "end": 3703,
      "text": "focusing only on the tight races of 'swing' states.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u50",
      "start": 3704,
      "end": 3826,
      "text": "During the 2000 campaign, seventeen states didn't see the candidates at all, including Rhode Island and South Carolina...\"",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u51",
      "start": 3827,
      "end": 3923,
      "text": "Swing states, as the're called, are the places where presidential candidates always hang around.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u52",
      "start": 3924,
      "end": 3964,
      "text": "They barely bother with the other states",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u53",
      "start": 3965,
      "end": 4032,
      "text": "because they know they have already got or lost the vote in them...",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u54",
      "start": 4034,
      "end": 4068,
      "text": "Some laws were brilliantly passed,",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u55",
      "start": 4069,
      "end": 4136,
      "text": "but had to eventually be deconstructed due to present implications.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u56",
      "start": 4137,
      "end": 4177,
      "text": "The electoral college is not democratic,",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u57",
      "start": 4178,
      "end": 4210,
      "text": "doesn't produce reliale results,",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u58",
      "start": 4211,
      "end": 4234,
      "text": "and discourages voters.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u59",
      "start": 4235,
      "end": 4274,
      "text": "It is time that we abolish this college",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u60",
      "start": 4275,
      "end": 4329,
      "text": "just at we overturned the eighteenth amendment before.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    }
  ],
